@topic stations
@title Workstations
@level 2
@related crafting,building,ancient
> Workbench      4 planks; tools, chests, beds, furnaces, clothes, boats
> Furnace        8 cobblestone at a workbench; ingots, glass, bricks, charcoal
> Campfire       3 sticks + 3 cobblestone; cooking (also a light source)
> Anvil          5 iron ingots + 2 stone bricks; iron tools, armour, the portal core
> Ancient Altar  6 ancient bricks + 4 aether shards at a workbench; starmetal gear, elixirs, lanterns
Place a station with R and stand within 3 cells (one level up or down is fine). Pressing E on a station opens crafting.

@topic farming
@title Farming and Trees
@level 2
@related crafting,time,weather
Hold a hoe and press U to till the grass or dirt in front of you into farmland. Select seeds and press R to plant them on the farmland.
> Wheat seeds  from tall grass (12%) or ripe wheat
> Potatoes     from ferns (6%); plant a potato to grow more
Crops grow in stages (about 4 game hours per wheat stage, 5 for potatoes). Rain speeds growth by a quarter, winter halves it, and crops covered by a solid block wait for light. Mine a ripe crop to harvest it: wheat gives wheat and two seeds, potatoes give three potatoes.

Leaves sometimes drop saplings (10%). Planted saplings grow into a tree trunk with a canopy after about half a day, if the space above is free.

@topic chests
@title Chests
@level 2
@related inventory,stations
Craft a chest (8 planks at a workbench) and place it with R. Face it and press E to open it. The left side is the chest (27 slots), the right side your inventory.
> Tab / Left / Right  switch side
> Enter               move the selected stack to the other side
> A                   move everything
Breaking a chest drops its contents. Chests are saved with the world.

@topic equipment
@title Equipment and Bags
@level 2
@related inventory,survival,combat
Clothes, armour and bags are worn in five slots: head, body, legs, feet and back. Select an item in the inventory and press W (or hold it and press U) to wear it; select a worn item at the bottom of the inventory list and press Enter or W to take it off.
> Fiber clothes   warmth +1..+4, little defense
> Leather armour  defense 4-12%, a little warmth
> Iron armour     defense 8-20% each, slightly cold
> Fiber bag       +15 kg carry capacity
Defense reduces damage (up to 80%). Warmth raises the felt temperature in the cold. Worn items count toward your weight.

@topic sleep
@title Sleeping
@level 2
@related survival,time,effects
Craft a bed (3 planks + 3 cloth at a workbench), place it and press E while facing it. You can sleep at night or whenever fatigue is above 60%. You sleep until half an hour after sunrise (at most 12 hours); during the day a tired player takes a nap instead.

While you sleep fatigue falls, health slowly returns and hunger and thirst drop at half speed; the world keeps going (weather, crops). Sleeping sets your spawn point to the bed and makes you Rested. You cannot sleep with hostile creatures within 12 cells.

@topic effects
@title Injuries, Illness and Buffs
@level 3
@related survival,sleep,crafting
Status effects are shown on the status panel and last a number of game minutes.
> Bleeding          -1 HP per minute; heavy falls, claws and teeth; cure: bandage
> Fracture          slower movement; falls of 7+ blocks; cure: splint
> Food poisoning    hunger, thirst and stamina loss; raw mushrooms and raw meat; cure: charcoal pill
> Poisoned          health loss; spiders, scorpions, void wisps; cure: charcoal pill
> Common cold       weak stamina regeneration, feels colder; after 30 minutes of hypothermia; cure: herbal tea
> Wet               feels 4 C colder; swimming or rain outdoors
> Well fed          better stamina regeneration; bread, stew
> Rested            better stamina regeneration; sleeping
> Ancient Blessing  fast stamina regeneration, warmth; ancient relics, aether elixir
Use a medicine with U, or /treat to use a fitting one. Effects are defined in data/effects/effects.def.

@topic buckets
@title Buckets
@level 2
@related fluids,crafting
Craft a bucket from 3 iron ingots at an anvil. Hold it and press U while facing water or lava to scoop up that whole cell; press R to pour it out again in front of you. A bucket remembers how much it carries (1-15 levels), so water is never duplicated, except when you scoop from the sea, which refills.

@topic structures
@title Mines and Ruins
@level 2
@related caves,items,chests
The world hides structures generated from the seed:
> Abandoned mines  underground (height 16-44): two long crossing corridors with branches, wooden ceiling beams, torches and mine crates at the corridor ends.
> Stone ruins      on dry land: a broken ring of cobblestone with an old crate in the middle.
Opening a crate for the first time fills it with loot (coal, ores, ingots, tools, food, cloth, seeds, rarely gems). /findstructure abandoned_mine shows the nearest one (cheat).

@topic ai
@title Creature Behaviour
@level 4
@related monsters,stealth,formulas
Every creature runs a goal-driven state machine; twice a second it picks the most urgent goal:
> 1 survive   badly hurt and sees you: flee
> 2 attack    hostile and perceives you: chase, then attack
> 3 shelter   burns in daylight: look for cover
> 4 home      NPCs walk home at dusk and sleep there
> 5 rest      day animals sleep at night, night creatures by day
> 6 wander    otherwise wander or stand still (less in rain)
Perception: sight = sight radius x weather visibility, halved in the dark for day animals and reduced by a third (more with Stealth) while you crouch; hearing = hearing radius x your noise %. Sleeping creatures perceive half as far. Attacking any creature makes it remember you (defensive creatures fight back).
Pathfinding: when the straight way is blocked, a chasing or homeward creature searches a route with A* (up one block, down three, 24 cells around it) and follows it; walls with a gap no longer stop them.
States shown by /mobs: idle, wandering, chasing, attacking, fleeing, sleeping, going home, seeking shelter. A red background marks a creature that is chasing or attacking you; sleeping creatures are dark grey.

@topic difficulty
@title Difficulty
@level 2
@related monsters,combat
> Peaceful  no monsters; hostile animals still defend themselves
> Easy      monsters deal 50% damage, fewer creatures
> Normal    100% damage (default)
> Hard      150% damage, more creatures
Change it any time with /difficulty <name>; switching to Peaceful removes all monsters. The difficulty is saved with the world. /spawning off stops natural spawning (cheat).

@topic trading
@title Trading
@level 2
@related monsters,items
Face an NPC and press E (or use /trade). If you carry what one of its offers asks for, the trade happens at once; otherwise the NPC lists its offers in the message log.
> Wandering Trader  coal for trade tokens, tokens for bread or iron ingots
> Hermit            leather for bandages, raw meat for herbal tea, gems for tokens
> Old Miner         raw iron for an iron pickaxe, bread for torches, crystal shards for tokens
NPCs are defensive: they fight back if you attack them. Pressing E on an animal or monster shows what it is doing.

@topic sailing
@title Sailing
@level 2
@related ships,wind,shipdamage,skills
Aboard, the movement keys steer: the key in the direction of the bow raises the throttle (0-3), the opposite key lowers it (to -1 = backwards for ships with oars), a sideways key turns the bow that way if there is room. /anchor stops the ship.
> Oars    speed from your arms: costs stamina for every cell
> Sails   speed from the wind: full in a tailwind, 75% on a broad reach, 45% across the wind, 15% into it
The faster of both counts. Overloading halves the speed, flooding slows the ship. Every 8 cells train Sailing, which adds 1% speed per level. The status panel shows ship, hull, flooding %, throttle and speed. /shipinfo shows everything, /wind the wind.

@topic shipdamage
@title Hull Damage and Sinking
@level 3
@related ships,sailing,weather,formulas
Every ship has hull points and three damage stages:
> Intact    above 66%
> Damaged   34-66%: leaks 1 litre per second (yellow hull)
> Critical  33% or less: leaks 4 litres per second (red hull)
Waves damage the hull when the wind is stronger than the ship can take (raft 40%, rowing boat 55%, sailing boat 70%, merchant ship 85%): storms are dangerous for small boats. Running aground faster than 30 cells per 100 ticks costs hull points. Rain and overloading let water in.

Water in the hull is shown in percent; above 50% the hull turns blue. The ship sinks when it is full (capacity / 4 litres), when its hull reaches 0, or when cargo + water exceed 150% of its capacity. A sinking ship releases its cargo and some wreckage as floating items. Bail (U or /bail; a bucket in hand bails three times as much) and repair in time. Creaking and cracking sounds warn you.

@topic wind
@title Wind
@level 3
@related sailing,weather
The wind strength comes from the weather (clear 10%, rain 30%, thunderstorm 60%, windy 80%, storm 95%), its direction drifts slowly. /wind shows both; the direction is where the wind blows to. Sailing ships are fastest with the wind behind them and almost stop when sailing into it. Strong wind raises waves that damage small hulls.

@topic portal
@title Portals
@level 2
@related ancient,crafting
Craft a Portal Core at an anvil (4 obsidian, 6 crystal shards, 2 gems, 2 gold ingots, Crafting 5) and place it with R: it becomes an Ancient Portal. Face it and press E to travel. You arrive at the same x/z in the other dimension, on the nearest dry land within 48 cells; a return portal is built east of you unless one stands within 8 cells. Ships, creatures and items stay behind.

Obsidian forms where water meets lava (or in deep lava caves). Breaking a portal returns its core. If you die, you respawn in the dimension of your spawn point (sleeping in a bed sets it).

@topic ancientbiomes
@title Ancient Biomes
@level 3
@related ancient,biomes
> Ancient Grassland   magenta grass, star flowers, lone elder trees
> Ancient Forest      dense elder woods with glowing leaves
> Forgotten Garden    warm and humid, every kind of glowing plant
> Crystal Wilds       highlands of crystal turf and crystal blooms
> Silent Swamp        silent mud, moonreed and glowcaps
> Starlight Plain     dry fields of glowing star sand
> Ancient Sanctuary   brick-paved ground, guarded
> Void Rift           chasms falling 40 blocks to a floor of void stone; no water

@topic waypoints
@title Waypoints and Navigation
@level 2
@related commands,saving
Save up to 16 named places with /waypoint add <name>; /waypoint list shows them with their dimension, /waypoint remove <name> deletes one. /navigate <name> tells the direction and distance, /compass points to your spawn point, /deathpoint shows where you died last, /distance <x> <z> measures. Waypoints are saved with the world; /gowaypoint <name> teleports (cheat).

@topic fishing
@title Fishing
@level 2
@related skills,ocean,crafting
Craft a fishing rod (3 sticks + 2 string). Hold it, face water and press U to cast; after 3-8 seconds something bites. The catch chance is 35% + Fishing level / 2 + Luck / 4: usually raw fish, sometimes a bone, and in the Ancient Dimension rarely an ancient relic. Moving or pressing U again reels the line in. Every cast trains Fishing (more on a catch) and costs the rod one point of durability. Cook fish at a campfire.
